<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_WastelandBrineWater.xml             UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-18
  ============================================================================
  FISH_BESTIARY_BUILD_1 wave 2 — the Wasteland's "hypersaline pools" (§2G,
  wasteland.md §4/§10: "sealed dead-river termini... three hypersaline
  pools"). Same crib shape as RUT_ScaldWater.xml (this same folder): four
  TerrainDefs standing in for the water RUT_Wasteland actually generates, so
  the biome's own def can point at them instead of falling back to a vanilla
  default.

  🔴 CORRECTS wave 1's own finding (RUT_WastelandBrine_Items.xml header,
  FISH_BESTIARY_BUILD_1). Wave 1 read the DONOR `Wasteland` BiomeDef
  (Mlie.AdvancedBiomes, workshop 3541022508) and found its water fields wired
  to Odyssey's ToxicWater* family (waterBodyType Other, fishing dead per
  Verse.WaterBody.SetFishTypes()). That donor def is NOT what the live
  campaign map paints: MEASURED via world/ASHKARR_WORLDMAP_tiles.csv (proper
  csv.DictReader column read, not a scan) — `RUT_Wasteland` covers all 1853
  Wasteland-region tiles, defName "Wasteland" (bare) covers ZERO. `RUT_Wasteland`
  itself (RUT_Wasteland.xml, this folder) sets NONE of waterDeepTerrain/
  waterShallowTerrain/waterMovingShallowTerrain/waterMovingChestDeepTerrain,
  so per Verse/MapGenUtility.cs:182 (`map.BiomeAt(cell).waterDeepTerrain ??
  TerrainDefOf.WaterDeep`) any water on a live RUT_Wasteland map before this
  file was plain vanilla FRESHWATER — fishing there would in fact have
  worked. The "engine-dead" finding was real, just for a def nothing on the
  planet uses.
  This does NOT reopen fishing as the delivery mechanism: the owner ruled
  (2026-09-18, relayed to this build) that mining the pool floor is the
  brine-battery archetype's mechanism regardless — "the pool you want to
  mine has one, and it is a capacitor" is the spec's OWN flavor line
  (§4.3), not a workaround invented to route around the engine bug. This
  file exists so RUT_Wasteland's water has a terrain of its own to mine INTO
  (see RUT_WastelandBrineDeposits.xml) and to carry the hypersaline flavor
  (water_taxonomy.csv "waste_brine": "dead-river concentrate;
  radiologically live") the biome's own description already claims for
  every drop of water on it ("everything they carried is concentrated into
  salt and brine").

  Based on Odyssey's ToxicWater*Base family (not vanilla WaterBase, unlike
  the Scald): matches the donor's own choice for this archetype and the
  water_taxonomy.csv flavor ("radiologically live"), and NOT wiring
  fishTypes onto RUT_Wasteland means the ToxicWater* waterBodyType=Other
  "no fish" trait is inert here rather than a second copy of wave 1's bug.
  MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey" throughout, matching RUT_Tekk/
  RUT_Drazz's own gating (wave 1).

  Scope: RUT_Wasteland is "one def, by ruling" (RUT_Wasteland.xml's own
  header) for the whole biome family (dayside basins/margin/dark scour), so
  wiring these onto it applies to ANY water RUT_Wasteland generates on ANY
  of its 1853 tiles, not narrowly to three hand-placed tiles — the SS8
  mutator/injection palette that would scope "hypersaline pool" to specific
  tiles is its own future authoring pass (RUT_Wasteland.xml's own "NOT this
  pass's scope" list) and is not built here. This is the same scope wave 1
  already accepted for the (never-wired) fishTypes plan.

  RUT_WastelandBrineShallow tag added to the two shallow variants only
  (Shallow/MovingShallow) — GenStep_ScatterThings.CanScatterAt is TAG-based
  (Verse/GenStep_ScatterThings.cs, verified this pass), same resolved finding
  RUT_ScaldWater.xml already cites for RUT_ScaldShallow. Deep/chest-deep
  variants do not carry it: deposits sit in the shallows a pawn can actually
  stand in, not the open pool center (also ToxicWaterDeepBase is
  Impassable — nothing can be scattered or mined there at all).
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <TerrainDef ParentName="ToxicWaterDeepBase" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
    <defName>RUT_WastelandBrineDeep</defName>
    <label>hypersaline deep water</label>
    <description>Deep brine, dead-river salt and the war's own leavings concentrated past any use. Nothing swims here that was not built for it.</description>
    <renderPrecedence>395</renderPrecedence>
    <tags>
      <li>Water</li>
    </tags>
  </TerrainDef>

  <TerrainDef ParentName="ToxicWaterChestDeepBase" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
    <defName>RUT_WastelandBrineMovingChestDeep</defName>
    <label>hypersaline chest-deep water</label>
    <description>Fast, chest-deep brine feeding one of the dead rivers' last stretches before the salt takes it. Corrosive at length, not on contact.</description>
    <renderPrecedence>399</renderPrecedence>
    <affordances>
      <li>Bridgeable</li>
      <li>Walkable</li>
      <li>MovingFluid</li>
    </affordances>
    <waterDepthShader>Map/WaterDepth</waterDepthShader>
    <waterDepthShaderParameters>
      <_UseWaterOffset>1</_UseWaterOffset>
    </waterDepthShaderParameters>
    <tags>
      <li>Water</li>
      <li>River</li>
    </tags>
  </TerrainDef>

  <TerrainDef ParentName="ToxicWaterShallowBase" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
    <defName>RUT_WastelandBrineShallow</defName>
    <label>hypersaline shallow water</label>
    <description>The margin of a brine pool, salt-crusted at the edge, mineral beds visible through the shallows. The pool's owner lives somewhere under this crust.</description>
    <renderPrecedence>394</renderPrecedence>
    <tags>
      <li>Water</li>
      <li>RUT_WastelandBrineShallow</li>
    </tags>
  </TerrainDef>

  <TerrainDef ParentName="ToxicWaterShallowBase" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
    <defName>RUT_WastelandBrineMovingShallow</defName>
    <label>hypersaline shallow moving water</label>
    <description>A dying river's last shallow reach, running slower with every tile toward the pool it feeds. Salt-crusted at the margin, mineral beds visible underneath.</description>
    <renderPrecedence>398</renderPrecedence>
    <affordances>
      <li>ShallowWater</li>
      <li>WaterproofConduitable</li>
      <li>Bridgeable</li>
      <li>Walkable</li>
      <li>MovingFluid</li>
    </affordances>
    <waterDepthShader>Map/WaterDepth</waterDepthShader>
    <waterDepthShaderParameters>
      <_UseWaterOffset>1</_UseWaterOffset>
    </waterDepthShaderParameters>
    <tags>
      <li>Water</li>
      <li>River</li>
      <li>RUT_WastelandBrineShallow</li>
    </tags>
  </TerrainDef>

</Defs>
